-- ext:[SH 2307 p.992, read from the page image] | כתוצאה מפגיעת איבה לפני יום התחילה; תגמולים והטבות לפי החוק העיקרי כנוסחו
-- ext:[SH 2307 p.992, read from the page image] | ספר החוקים 2307, כ"ו בתמוז התשע"א, 28.7.2011 [printed page 992]
-- ext:[SH 2307 p.993, read from the page image] | (ג) יתום משני הוריו שנפטרו כתוצאה מפגיעת איבה לפני יום ב' בתשרי התשס"א (1
-- ext:[SH 2307 p.993, read from the page image] | באוקטובר 2000), ובמועד שבו התייתם טרם מלאו לו 37 שנים, יהא זכאי
-- ext:[SH 2307 p.993, read from the page image] | למענק מיוחד בסכום של 550,000 שקלים חדשים, ובלבד שביום התחילה מלאו לו
-- ext:[SH 2307 p.993, read from the page image] | 21 שנים; הוראות סעיף קטן זה יחולו, בשינויים המחויבים, גם לגבי יתום משני הוריו
-- ext:[SH 2307 p.993, read from the page image] | שחלות לגביו הוראות סעיף 9ב(ב) לחוק משפחות חיילים, כנוסחו בחוק זה.
-- ext:[SH 2307 p.993, read from the page image] | ספר החוקים 2307, כ"ו בתמוז התשע"א, 28.7.2011 [printed page 993]
-- The instrument that inserted subsection (ד1) into section 4 of the 2011 instrument was not found among the pages the row holds, and the row does not say which it is.
-- The consolidation's line is not word for word the instrument's (ד2): the consolidation adds the words that put the death before the commencement of "this law" and a figure 37, and does not say "in addition to the grants under (ג) and (ד1)".
-- The row records both placements and does not say that the two are one grant.

GIVEN a IS A `A grant and where a text puts it`
      b IS A `A grant and where a text puts it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two texts put the grant in the same law` MEANS a's `the law it is put in` EQUALS b's `the law it is put in`

GIVEN a IS A `A grant and where a text puts it`
      b IS A `A grant and where a text puts it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two texts put the grant in the same section` MEANS a's `the section it is put in` EQUALS b's `the section it is put in`

GIVEN a IS A `A grant and where a text puts it`
      b IS A `A grant and where a text puts it`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the two amounts agree` MEANS a's `the amount in new shekels` EQUALS b's `the amount in new shekels`

`the 200,000-shekel grant as the consolidation prints it` MEANS
    `A grant and where a text puts it` WITH
        `the amount in new shekels` IS 200000
        `the law it is put in` IS "Compensation to Victims of Hostile Actions Law, 5730-1970"
        `the section it is put in` IS "4א"
        `the subsection it is put in` IS "(ד1)"
        `put there by` IS "the consolidation (revision 3037611 of the Hebrew Wikisource page), line 84 of the whole page, under the heading line 69"
        `read from` IS `the consolidation only`

`the 200,000-shekel grant as the 2016 instrument inserts it` MEANS
    `A grant and where a text puts it` WITH
        `the amount in new shekels` IS 200000
        `the law it is put in` IS "Compensation to Victims of Hostile Actions (Amendment 30) Law, 5771-2011"
        `the section it is put in` IS "4"
        `the subsection it is put in` IS "(ד2)"
        `put there by` IS "section 1 of the instrument printed in Sefer HaChukim 2573, printed p. 1160"
        `read from` IS `an official instrument, read from its page image`

`the 550,000-shekel grant in subsection (ג) of s 4 of the 2011 instrument` MEANS
    `A grant and where a text puts it` WITH
        `the amount in new shekels` IS 550000
        `the law it is put in` IS "Compensation to Victims of Hostile Actions (Amendment 30) Law, 5771-2011"
        `the section it is put in` IS "4"
        `the subsection it is put in` IS "(ג)"
        `put there by` IS "the instrument printed in Sefer HaChukim 2307, printed p. 993"
        `read from` IS `an official instrument, read from its page image`

§ `Printed date pairs`

GIVEN p IS A `A printed date pair`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the printed pair matches the routine` MEANS p's `the Gregorian date printed with it` EQUALS p's `the Gregorian date the calendar routine gives`

-- Each Hebrew date below was converted with the Hebrew-calendar routine in tools/hebcal.py (tools/datepairs.py runs the conversions and the routine's own control, 30 Kislev 5785 = 31 December 2024, first).
-- Each pair is on the footer line of the page named, or (the last) in the text of printed p. 993: the ext lines above.
`date pair: the footer of printed p. 614 of Sefer HaChukim 3072` MEANS
    `A printed date pair` WITH
        `the Hebrew date, transliterated` IS "14 Av 5783"
        `the Gregorian date printed with it` IS Date 1 8 2023
        `the Gregorian date the calendar routine gives` IS Date 1 8 2023
        `the pair was read from` IS `an official instrument, read from its page image`

